1
00:00:04,380 --> 00:00:08,120
I really did something
terrible to Volvo-san yesterday.

2
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:10,180
Don't worry about it.

3
00:00:10,180 --> 00:00:13,680
Thanks to that, we won't have to
be trained by that armed instructor.

4
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:18,040
If we were taught by that man,
we'd need more than one life.

5
00:00:18,040 --> 00:00:18,960
Fantasia

6
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:20,500
Get Maurin

7
00:00:21,680 --> 00:00:23,980
Yesterday was rude of me.

8
00:00:23,980 --> 00:00:26,860
Why are you here?

9
00:00:26,860 --> 00:00:28,940
Weren't you supposed to be hospitalized?

10
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,220
Being hospitalized for a scratch like this?

11
00:00:32,220 --> 00:00:34,280
After falling from such a high place...

12
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:35,800
I work out, you know.

13
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,260
You're not even human.

14
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:40,420
I'm sorry about yesterday.

15
00:00:41,100 --> 00:00:42,540
Don't worry about it.

16
00:00:42,960 --> 00:00:44,480
I thought it was strange too.

17
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:46,640
Even though she's this beautiful, she didn't get a nosebleed,
so

18
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:48,900
Anyway, now that we know Maria is a man,

19
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,000
you should train with
Mr. Ryotsu and the others

20
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,220
and get some training in.

21
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:55,300
No thanks, I'll pass.

22
00:00:55,300 --> 00:00:56,460
Don't hold back!

23
00:00:56,460 --> 00:00:59,080
With punching power like that, if you trained him,
he could even become a Green Beret,

24
00:01:05,740 --> 00:01:09,820
What the hell, Jonker?
Didn't I tell you not to sneak up behind me?

25
00:01:10,760 --> 00:01:14,080
Sorry, an airmail from America arrived, so

26
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:15,180
America

27
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:16,820
This is

28
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,020
What's wrong? Her face suddenly went pale.

29
00:01:22,020 --> 00:01:23,720
It's a chain letter, isn't it?

30
00:01:24,500 --> 00:01:25,380
It's worse than that.

31
00:01:29,180 --> 00:01:32,100
Colonel Bakuryu is coming,
and today of all days.

32
00:01:32,100 --> 00:01:34,380
Colonel Bakuryu? Who's that?

33
00:01:35,700 --> 00:01:39,340
He's Volvo-san's superior. A self-made
soldier who's survived countless crises.

34
00:01:39,860 --> 00:01:45,320
That'll be quite a sight. Since he's Volvo's superior,
he might turn out to be some outrageous pervert.

35
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:48,880
Yeah, right. It's no laughing matter.

36
00:01:49,300 --> 00:01:55,420
He's so tough they call him the Demon Sergeant.
It's not transport training, it's the colonel's training, you know.

37
00:01:55,420 --> 00:02:00,260
His strictness is no joke. Even I have
thought about deserting so many times.

38
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:04,040
The Colonel's unit is probably
the strongest in the world.

39
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:05,740
T-the man himself!

40
00:02:06,720 --> 00:02:08,100
We can't just stand here!

41
00:02:08,440 --> 00:02:09,760
Don't tear off your arm!

42
00:02:09,760 --> 00:02:11,400
Everyone, assemble in the classroom!

43
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,320
Aren't those bulletproof vests?

44
00:02:15,820 --> 00:02:17,500
You two should change too.

45
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:19,780
Isn't that a bit much, though?

46
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:23,540
You can say that because you don't
know how terrifying the Colonel is.

47
00:02:24,060 --> 00:02:26,740
After all,
he's the type who shoots as a greeting.

48
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:28,940
Don't blame me if a stray bullet hits you.

49
00:02:30,420 --> 00:02:32,760
Anyway,
you might as well change like he said.

50
00:02:32,760 --> 00:02:34,240
Like Honda-san did.

51
00:02:34,240 --> 00:02:36,740
Quick, aren't you?

52
00:02:37,920 --> 00:02:39,560
I want to go home.

53
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:55,800
Bringing out rocket launchers
and even a Vulcan cannon,

54
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:57,440
are you planning to start a war?

55
00:02:57,840 --> 00:02:59,040
Even this isn't enough yet.

56
00:03:00,260 --> 00:03:00,700
We're still short.

57
00:03:00,700 --> 00:03:03,500
This music is

58
00:03:03,500 --> 00:03:05,440
Wagner's "Ride of the Valkyries."

59
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:07,940
Why's it coming from outside?

60
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:09,820
The colonel must have arrived.

61
00:03:10,260 --> 00:03:11,140
That's a helicopter.

62
00:03:11,140 --> 00:03:11,920
Just as I thought.

63
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:16,080
Isn't it a media helicopter?

64
00:03:19,060 --> 00:03:19,600
That one is

65
00:03:20,380 --> 00:03:21,800
an Apache!

66
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:36,740
Why would a US military
aircraft be way out here?

67
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:38,300
It's coming this way!

68
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:42,240
Everyone, get against the wall!

69
00:03:55,460 --> 00:03:57,420
Firing off a volley out of nowhere!

70
00:03:57,420 --> 00:03:58,600
Didn't I tell you?

71
00:04:00,320 --> 00:04:00,800
Stop it!

72
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:03,920
Nyaaaaaah!

73
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:08,060
Damn! Did we miss?

74
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:09,600
What have you done?!

75
00:04:09,760 --> 00:04:12,860
It's the Colonel we're talking about! He'll come back ten times,
no, a hundred times worse!

76
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:17,760
Hurry and run!

77
00:04:20,740 --> 00:04:21,600
Run!

78
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:49,780
Eeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee!

79
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:51,920
It was to protect you! I didn't attack!

80
00:04:53,440 --> 00:04:56,120
They've landed, though.

81
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:26,000
Volgo Saigo, long time no see.

82
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:27,500
So this is the colonel?

83
00:05:30,020 --> 00:05:31,900
It's been a long time, Colonel.

84
00:05:31,900 --> 00:05:35,000
The uniform suits you, as always.

85
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:35,660
Hello.

86
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:38,860
You're too lenient, Saigo.

87
00:05:42,080 --> 00:05:43,460
He actually shot at us!

88
00:05:43,460 --> 00:05:44,820
He's a terrifying man.

89
00:05:46,760 --> 00:05:48,380
Your moves are passable.

90
00:05:48,380 --> 00:05:51,420
But that won't make you a real soldier.

91
00:05:51,420 --> 00:05:52,700
We're not soldiers.

92
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:55,440
Get out of the way!
Are you planning to defy your superior?

93
00:05:55,600 --> 00:05:57,500
I never considered you my superior!

94
00:05:57,960 --> 00:05:58,540
Shut up!

95
00:06:02,200 --> 00:06:03,540
Don't you dare talk back!

96
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:08,140
Damn it! You went and wrecked the training grounds.
That's going too far!

97
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:11,379
Any sparks that fall on me,
I crush completely.

98
00:06:11,429 --> 00:06:13,300
That's the iron rule for survival.

99
00:06:14,380 --> 00:06:16,100
Still, what a terrible scar.

100
00:06:17,200 --> 00:06:19,760
Young lady, you've noticed something good.

101
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,420
The face is just a tiny part of it.

102
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,040
These scars are my history.

103
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:26,080
Wow.

104
00:06:26,820 --> 00:06:28,900
This is where I was shot in the Vietnam War.

105
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:31,240
This is a scar from the Falklands War.

106
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:33,080
This is from the Iran war.

107
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:34,080
And then,

108
00:06:34,580 --> 00:06:34,940
and then,

109
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,180
this one is

110
00:06:37,760 --> 00:06:38,360
that one is

111
00:06:39,280 --> 00:06:41,400
scratch marks from my wife.

112
00:06:43,520 --> 00:06:46,480
Sabu! He's doing some kind of bit.

113
00:06:46,480 --> 00:06:49,040
After such a long setup,
that's a pretty typical punchline, isn't it?

114
00:06:49,040 --> 00:06:51,700
The type who always has to tack
a punchline onto stories like that.

115
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:59,220
I wonder... I was thinking that...
Right?
Sorry, I'm not doing it. This is the Colonel's...

116
00:06:59,220 --> 00:07:00,840
It's a box, I thought it was.

117
00:07:03,960 --> 00:07:06,840
In the end, you only got hurt because you're weak,
isn't that right?

118
00:07:06,840 --> 00:07:13,060
Well, what a thing to say. You've got quite a bit of courage,
don't you?

119
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:17,020
It's not that much.
What's this lawbreaker's name?

120
00:07:17,020 --> 00:07:18,040
My name is Ryotsu.

121
00:07:18,040 --> 00:07:19,460
Mister Ryotsu.

122
00:07:19,460 --> 00:07:21,300
You're fearless, aren't you?

123
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:22,940
Daring to talk back to me like this!

124
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:25,840
I'll give you something wonderful.

125
00:07:25,840 --> 00:07:26,960
What is it?

126
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,420
It's the greatest gift.

127
00:07:29,420 --> 00:07:30,140
Me.

128
00:07:30,140 --> 00:07:31,680
On my back.

129
00:07:31,680 --> 00:07:34,420
What did you put in? What? Tell me.

130
00:07:34,420 --> 00:07:39,560
See that? The power of a hand grenade!

131
00:07:39,560 --> 00:07:41,880
This is what happens when you make me angry.

132
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:44,860
Maybe I cut the gunpowder a little too much.

133
00:07:44,860 --> 00:07:47,600
Maybe I should've used a bit more.

134
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:50,040
Dumbass, we're not kids!

135
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:52,300
Don't use it like a Nee-Beeder.

136
00:07:52,300 --> 00:07:54,340
By the way, Colonel, why are you here?

137
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,400
Right. I totally forgot.

138
00:07:56,400 --> 00:07:57,040
Hey.

139
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:18,200
Yes, I'm Ryotsu. Nice to meet you.

140
00:08:18,200 --> 00:08:20,060
I'm Honda.

141
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:22,020
I'm Volvo.

142
00:08:22,020 --> 00:08:23,900
Nice to meet you, I'm Jodie.

143
00:08:23,900 --> 00:08:25,900
Jodie is my daughter, you know.

144
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:29,940
It's true, I'm her mom.

145
00:08:29,940 --> 00:08:31,000
I see.

146
00:08:33,140 --> 00:08:35,740
Actually, for Jodie's husband,

147
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:39,540
I chose you.

148
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:41,340
Nice to meet you.

149
00:08:41,340 --> 00:08:43,320
Mushi-kun, Chu-kun.

150
00:08:44,400 --> 00:08:45,660
I've heard all about you.

151
00:08:47,140 --> 00:08:48,920
Think it over carefully, Volvo!

152
00:08:48,920 --> 00:08:52,500
Even if she's a blonde bombshell,
her father is that guy!

153
00:08:53,200 --> 00:08:54,500
Now that you mention it...

154
00:08:54,500 --> 00:08:58,500
Saigo, are you really going
to waste this nice body?

155
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:02,400
And if you marry her,

156
00:09:02,400 --> 00:09:06,200
you'll get your Yankees Stadium
senior's land thrown in too!

157
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:09,200
Your Yankees Stadium senior!

158
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:11,820
Colonel,
please give me your daughter's hand.

159
00:09:11,820 --> 00:09:14,920
Don't apologize.
There are plenty of other candidates.

160
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:17,660
I plan to make my final
decision from among them.

161
00:09:18,120 --> 00:09:18,520
I see.

162
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,460
A man must be strong. That is my creed.

163
00:09:22,920 --> 00:09:27,060
I intend to choose a husband
from the strong men I know.

164
00:09:27,060 --> 00:09:29,280
But Volvo hates women, you know.

165
00:09:29,280 --> 00:09:30,660
How could you say such a thing!

166
00:09:30,660 --> 00:09:33,380
Colonel, when it comes to strength,
I'm confident too!

167
00:09:33,380 --> 00:09:34,700
Please, put me on the list!

168
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,580
Shamelessly pushing yourself like that.

169
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:37,380
Ryo-san!

170
00:09:39,200 --> 00:09:40,520
You're running too, right?

171
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:42,300
Me, I...

172
00:09:43,880 --> 00:09:44,440
Run!

173
00:09:46,720 --> 00:09:47,760
Ken-chan

174
00:09:47,760 --> 00:09:48,560
Mr. Nakagawa

175
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:51,700
They're rubber training bullets.

176
00:09:51,700 --> 00:09:54,560
Anyway, you're wearing a bulletproof vest,
aren't you?

177
00:09:54,980 --> 00:09:55,380
Right.

178
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:58,380
Whoever subdues the last one passes.

179
00:09:59,120 --> 00:09:59,920
Me too.

180
00:10:00,580 --> 00:10:02,920
What's with you young ladies' glee?

181
00:10:04,300 --> 00:10:05,560
I'm so frustrated.

182
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,160
He's just that kind of man.

183
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:08,260
Give up.

184
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:12,840
I'm fine, so I'll decline this time.

185
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:13,720
What did you say?!

186
00:10:14,400 --> 00:10:15,040
You bastard!

187
00:10:15,340 --> 00:10:16,640
Look closely, Frey!

188
00:10:16,660 --> 00:10:17,840
Bust 95

189
00:10:17,840 --> 00:10:19,660
Waist 58

190
00:10:19,660 --> 00:10:21,220
Hips 90

191
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:24,240
Are you saying you
don't like this nice body?

192
00:10:26,380 --> 00:10:28,740
But I have Otohime-chan

193
00:10:29,300 --> 00:10:32,940
Shan, are you trying to insult the daughter?

194
00:10:34,380 --> 00:10:35,880
Never, sir!

195
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:38,460
So you're passing me, then?

196
00:10:39,200 --> 00:10:41,120
Yes, absolutely, sir!

197
00:10:42,220 --> 00:10:44,600
Well, you could have
said that from the start.

198
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:46,560
Good luck.

199
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:49,881
Yes, Honda, Hayato,

200
00:10:49,931 --> 00:10:51,780
I'll do my best!

201
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:57,460
Alright! Then the three of you will go all
the way to Africa to take the final test!

202
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,340
What! Africa!

203
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:16,920
Now then, here in Africa,

204
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:20,900
I will hold a contest to choose
a husband for my daughter Jodie.

205
00:11:20,900 --> 00:11:23,680
You gentlemen were chosen
from among many candidates.

206
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,400
You are the cream of the crop,
the strongest of the strong.

207
00:11:25,400 --> 00:11:28,960
The one man who emerges from this
group as the strongest in the world

208
00:11:28,960 --> 00:11:31,060
will be promised marriage to Jodie.

209
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:34,580
This is the final battle:
the Africa-crossing ultra course!

210
00:11:35,040 --> 00:11:38,540
Whoever reaches the goal first by
running this course will be the winner.

211
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:42,194
The course cuts straight across the savanna from here,
crosses a river,

212
00:11:42,244 --> 00:11:44,576
then crosses the savanna
again and goes over the desert,

213
00:11:44,626 --> 00:11:46,480
and the goal is at the summit
of the mountain beyond that.

214
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,260
The total course length is 100 kilometers.

215
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:51,520
Well then, I wish you all the best of luck.

216
00:11:51,620 --> 00:11:52,280
Wait a minute!

217
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:53,560
What?

218
00:11:53,780 --> 00:11:55,686
An ultra-marathon across Africa,

219
00:11:55,736 --> 00:11:58,060
with only one knife for a weapon?
That's too reckless!

220
00:11:58,460 --> 00:12:00,460
Yeah, at least give us a rifle.

221
00:12:00,640 --> 00:12:04,316
Don't you dare go quiet on me! A truly
strong man needs nothing but a knife.

222
00:12:04,366 --> 00:12:07,120
Anyone who has a complaint is
disqualified right here and now.

223
00:12:07,120 --> 00:12:09,280
Okay, I'm fine with being disqualified.

224
00:12:09,280 --> 00:12:12,000
Good luck, everyone, and be careful!

225
00:12:14,700 --> 00:12:15,980
Yes, I'll do my best.

226
00:12:15,980 --> 00:12:20,540
If I win and get married, I'll get land a
thousand times the size of Yankee Stadium!

227
00:12:20,540 --> 00:12:22,800
So basically, I'll be a billionaire.

228
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,380
I can't quit now!

229
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:26,800
I'm the one who's definitely
going to become the groom!

230
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:28,560
I'm the true strongman here.

231
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,620
I can't lose this match, no matter what!

232
00:12:32,980 --> 00:12:35,080
Then take your positions.

233
00:12:36,080 --> 00:12:37,000
Ready... set!

234
00:12:47,720 --> 00:12:49,579
The course has mountains and valleys,

235
00:12:49,629 --> 00:12:52,060
and there may be some
unexpected pitfalls too.

236
00:12:55,620 --> 00:12:57,160
W-what the hell is this!

237
00:13:00,980 --> 00:13:01,720
Are you okay?

238
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:04,580
Look,

239
00:13:05,120 --> 00:13:06,920
But we just have to give it our all.

240
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:13,400
Senpai, if I really start to fall,

241
00:13:13,400 --> 00:13:14,860
you'll pull me back up, right?

242
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:16,300
Don't worry, just keep going.

243
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:17,180
I've got you.

244
00:13:20,180 --> 00:13:21,580
Whoa, that was close, that was close!

245
00:13:21,580 --> 00:13:23,620
So there were more
pitfalls than just the one

246
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:31,160
Senpai, the movie trap is over.

247
00:13:32,300 --> 00:13:33,160
Huff, huff!

248
00:13:33,540 --> 00:13:34,260
Haah!

249
00:13:34,440 --> 00:13:35,700
You liar!

250
00:13:36,480 --> 00:13:38,820
Never let your guard
down until the very end.

251
00:13:38,940 --> 00:13:40,780
Nahahahaha!

252
00:13:44,660 --> 00:13:57,260
What's wrong?

253
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:58,740
Let's look over there.

254
00:14:00,100 --> 00:14:01,680
Is that a log?

255
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,320
It's a pack of crocodiles!

256
00:14:14,700 --> 00:14:16,400
Sensei, let's go on an adventure

257
00:14:16,400 --> 00:14:18,740
We've come all the way to Africa,
there's no backing out of an adventure now!

258
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:22,920
I'm going!
I'll call it the White Rabbit of Inaba Plan!

259
00:14:24,920 --> 00:14:26,500
Aaaaah

260
00:14:27,440 --> 00:14:29,760
Ryotsu already went that way, so

261
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:30,960
Then I'll

262
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:31,400
Yeah

263
